# Append-only fleet docs: every relay job appends its own section at EOF, so two cards
# dispatched on this repo from the same base collide there even when their sections have
# nothing to do with each other (ghostwave PR #20: PLAN.md, 2026-10-21). The union driver
# keeps BOTH sides and writes no conflict markers, which is exactly how these conflicts have
# been resolved by hand — so it can never block a push, a PR, or a merge again.
#
# The fleet also fences this at the boundary: ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_rebase.sh merges
# origin/<default> into the card branch before push, and a pre-push hook refuses a branch
# that does not already contain origin/<default>. This file makes the doc half of that
# automatic. Real conflicts in source files are still real conflicts: resolve those, do not
# widen this rule to them.
PLAN.md     merge=union
PROGRESS.md merge=union
